{#
  One page as Markdown — shared by /llms-full.txt (every page, titles at ##) and the
  per-page {url}.md (one page, title at #). One place, so the two can't drift.

  page(entry, level) writes the page with its title at `level`; the body's own
  headings are demoted by level - 1 so they sit beneath it. Bodies are the fields the
  HTML pages render, converted by craft.frontend.markdown(): `content` (about, policy
  pages) and the caseContent blocks (case studies, notes, tools). Only blocks that
  carry words are written — images, video and lottie have nothing to read, and the
  homepage analysis form is a form. A quote keeps its attribution, code stays fenced,
  the method block becomes the methodology's phases.

  SECTIONS is the whole list of what has a Markdown version. Anything else — a VIP
  door above all — is not in it, and /{uri}.md 404s.

  Autoescape is off INSIDE every macro: a macro escapes in the context where it is
  defined, not where it is called (see llms.twig).
#}
{%- macro sections() -%}
    {{- 'homepage,about,caseStudy,caseStudies,note,notes,tools,pages,contact' -}}
{%- endmacro -%}

{#- The .md address of an entry that has one. The homepage's URI is `__home__` and its
    URL ends in a slash, so it gets /index.md rather than "/.md". -#}
{%- macro url(entry) -%}
    {{- entry.uri == '__home__' ? siteUrl('index.md') : entry.url ~ '.md' -}}
{%- endmacro -%}

{%- macro line(text) -%}
    {%- autoescape false -%}
        {{- (text ?? '')|striptags|split("\n\n")|first|trim|replace({"\n": ' ', "\r": ''}) -}}
    {%- endautoescape -%}
{%- endmacro -%}

{%- macro blocks(entry, shift) -%}
    {%- autoescape false -%}
    {%- for block in entry.caseContent.all() ?? [] -%}
        {%- set handle = block.type.handle -%}
        {%- if handle == 'content' -%}
            {%- set md = craft.frontend.markdown(block.content ?? '', shift) -%}
            {%- if md %}{{ md }}

{% endif -%}
        {%- elseif handle == 'code' and (block.codeSnippet ?? '')|trim -%}
```{{ block.codeLanguage ?? '' }}
{{ block.codeSnippet|trim }}
```

{% elseif handle == 'caseTestimonial' -%}
            {%- set quoted = block.testimonial.status(null).one() -%}
            {%- if quoted and (quoted.blockquote ?? '')|trim -%}
                {%- set who = [quoted.personName ?? '', quoted.jobTitle ?? '', craft.frontend.testimonialCompany(quoted)]|map(v => v|trim)|filter(v => v)|join(', ') -%}
> {{ quoted.blockquote|striptags|trim|replace({"\n\n": "\n>\n> ", "\n": "\n> "}) }}
{% if who %}>
> — {{ who }}
{% endif %}

{% endif -%}
        {%- elseif handle == 'contentMethod' -%}
            {%- for phase in craft.frontend.methodology() -%}
**{{ phase.title }}**{% if phase.summary %}: {{ phase.summary|striptags|trim }}{% endif %}{% if phase.services|length %} ({{ phase.services|join(', ') }}){% endif %}

{% endfor -%}
        {%- endif -%}
    {%- endfor -%}
    {%- endautoescape -%}
{%- endmacro -%}

{#- A list entry: `- [Title](url): one line`. -#}
{%- macro item(entry, text) -%}
    {%- import _self as f -%}
    {%- autoescape false -%}
    {%- set s = f.line(text) -%}
- [{{ entry.title }}]({{ entry.url }}){% if s %}: {{ s }}{% endif %}
    {%- endautoescape -%}
{%- endmacro -%}

{%- macro page(entry, level) -%}
    {%- import _self as f -%}
    {%- autoescape false -%}
    {%- set h = range(1, level)|map(i => '#')|join -%}
    {%- set shift = level - 1 -%}
    {%- set handle = entry.section.handle -%}
    {%- set title = handle == 'caseStudies' ? ((entry.longTitle ?? '')|trim ?: entry.title) : entry.title -%}

{{ h }} {{ handle == 'homepage' ? siteName : title }}

Source: {{ entry.url }}
{% if handle == 'caseStudies' -%}
    {%- set client = craft.frontend.caseStudyClientName(entry, true) -%}
    {%- set role = entry.skills.all()|map(s => s.title)|join(', ') -%}
    {%- set year = (entry.hasDateHidden ?? false) or not entry.postDate ? '' : entry.postDate|date('Y') ~ ((entry.isPresent ?? false) ? ' – present' : '') -%}
    {%- set sectors = entry.sectorSelector.all()|map(c => (c.longTitle ?? '')|trim ?: c.title)|join(', ') -%}
{% if client %}Client: {{ client }}
{% endif %}
{%- if role %}Role: {{ role }}
{% endif %}
{%- if year %}Year: {{ year }}
{% endif %}
{%- if sectors %}Sectors: {{ sectors }}
{% endif %}

{{ craft.frontend.markdown(entry.caseSummary ?? '', shift) }}

{{ f.blocks(entry, shift) }}
{%- elseif handle == 'notes' -%}
    {%- set topics = entry.topicSelector is defined ? entry.topicSelector.all()|map(t => t.title)|join(', ') : '' -%}
{% if entry.postDate %}Published: {{ entry.postDate|date('Y-m-d') }}
{% endif %}
{%- if topics %}Topics: {{ topics }}
{% endif %}

{{ f.line(entry.summary ?? '') }}

{{ f.blocks(entry, shift) }}
{%- elseif handle == 'tools' %}

{{ f.line(entry.summary ?? '') }}

{{ f.blocks(entry, shift) }}
{%- elseif handle in ['about', 'pages'] %}

{{ craft.frontend.markdown(entry.content ?? '', shift) }}

{{ f.blocks(entry, shift) }}
{%- elseif handle == 'contact' %}

The contact page has a form, and the homepage assistant can take a message too.
{% elseif handle == 'caseStudy' %}

{{ f.line(entry.summary ?? '') }}

{% for study in craft.entries().section('caseStudies').status('live').all() %}
{{ f.item(study, (study.seoMetaDescription ?? '') ?: (study.caseSummary ?? '')) }}
{% endfor %}
{%- elseif handle == 'note' %}

{{ f.line(entry.summary ?? '') }}

{% for note in craft.entries().section('notes').status('live').orderBy('postDate DESC').all() %}
{{ f.item(note, (note.summary ?? '') ?: (note.seoMetaDescription ?? '')) }}{% if note.postDate %} ({{ note.postDate|date('Y-m-d') }}){% endif %}

{% endfor %}
{%- elseif handle == 'homepage' %}
    {%- set about = craft.entries().section('about').status('live').one() %}

> {{ f.line(about.summary ?? '') }}

{{ f.line((entry.seoMetaDescription ?? '') ?: craft.entries().section('globals').one().seoMetaDescription ?? '') }}

The homepage has an assistant that answers questions about the work in Jon's own
voice. Every page it draws on is listed below; each has a Markdown version at its
address plus `.md`. The whole site in one file: {{ siteUrl('llms-full.txt') }}

{% for single in ['about', 'caseStudy', 'note', 'contact'] %}
{%- set e = craft.entries().section(single).status('live').one() -%}
{%- if e %}{{ f.item(e, single == 'contact' ? 'how to get in touch.' : (e.summary ?? '')) }}
{% endif %}
{%- endfor %}
{%- for tool in craft.entries().section('tools').status('live').all() %}{{ f.item(tool, tool.summary ?? '') }}
{% endfor %}
{%- endif %}
    {%- endautoescape -%}
{%- endmacro -%}
